-- A default naming something that is not in scope is reported once, as that,
-- on a record's field (p10 of TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md): a field's default
-- is checked once every name of the module is in scope, so a name that does not
-- resolve there is defined nowhere, and saying "must be a literal" as well was a
-- misleading second error.
--
-- On a rule's INPUT it is not: the signature is scanned before the definitions
-- after it are in scope, so `zzz` below may be a definition of this very file,
-- and the default gets the literal error and its hint as well. The three shapes
-- that name something in the file are in not-ok/tc/typically-non-literal-input.l4.

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY zzz
GIVETH A NUMBER
f MEANS x

DECLARE Gauge HAS
  level IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY yyy
